WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.584
In engineering a voltage is switched on or a short pulse arrives.

2
00:00:04.584 --> 00:00:11.952
Classical methods are awkward with such discontinuous sources, while the Laplace method handles them easily.

3
00:00:11.952 --> 00:00:17.390
In this part we treat steps, impulses and an RLC circuit.

4
00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:23.256
The Heaviside function u of t minus c is zero before c and one after.

5
00:00:23.256 --> 00:00:30.384
The second shifting theorem: the transform of a function delayed by c is e to the minus c s times F.

6
00:00:30.384 --> 00:00:36.456
The transform of the Dirac impulse delta of t minus c is e to the minus c s.

7
00:00:36.456 --> 00:00:40.958
Convolution corresponds to the product of transforms.

8
00:00:41.208 --> 00:00:47.904
An RLC circuit: inductance one, resistance two, capacitance zero point two.

9
00:00:47.904 --> 00:00:51.192
Ten volts are switched on at time zero.

10
00:00:51.192 --> 00:00:59.798
The charge satisfies q double prime plus two q prime plus five q equals ten, with zero initial conditions.

11
00:01:00.048 --> 00:01:05.328
Q equals ten over s times s squared plus two s plus five.

12
00:01:05.328 --> 00:01:12.936
Partial fractions: two over s minus two times s plus two over s plus one squared plus four.

13
00:01:12.936 --> 00:01:18.110
We completed the square in the denominator because there are no real roots.

14
00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:26.928
Back with the first shifting theorem: q equals two minus e to the minus t times two cosine two t plus sine two t.

15
00:01:26.928 --> 00:01:34.646
The impulse response, the original of the transfer function, is one half e to the minus t sine two t.

16
00:01:34.896 --> 00:01:40.632
On the graph the charge tends to two coulombs, the capacitance times the voltage.

17
00:01:40.632 --> 00:01:45.504
On the way it overshoots slightly and settles with damped oscillations,

18
00:01:45.504 --> 00:01:50.678
because the characteristic roots are complex with negative real part.

19
00:01:50.928 --> 00:01:56.832
Question: what is the original of e to the minus three s times capital F of s?

20
00:01:56.832 --> 00:01:59.880
Pause the video, choose your answer,

21
00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:05.558
then read the explanation and go back to the relevant part of the lesson if needed.
